00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.210
You are a cheerleader to these people.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.043
How excited are you?

00:03:10.043 --> 00:03:12.623
We're doing 'AGT All Stars'
right now, it's on tonight.

00:03:12.623 --> 00:03:13.456
(audience cheering)
- It's so incredible.

00:03:13.456 --> 00:03:14.790
It's incredible.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.200
Now, you have to understand.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.777
And I know you've given me
a great compliment here,

00:03:18.777 --> 00:03:21.720
but I have to tell you, I am a fan first.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.700
I am a fan of entertainers.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.030
The courage, I mean,
everything that it takes

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.700
to become an entertainer in this business.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.180
Be it dancing, singing,
comedy, all this stuff.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.660
I'm always gleaning
knowledge from every act

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.100
that comes on that show.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.590
Because they take me to another level.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:43.050
I'm literally watching
the courage that it takes

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.240
for a little 10 year old to go sing

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.950
in front of millions of people.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.810
I couldn't have done that when I was 10.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.100
And so, I look at this stuff and I'm like,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.690
I have to support it.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.160
I have to be behind it.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.702
And I want to give them
everything they need,

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.535
to be their best.
- [Howie] You give them

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.368
more than they need.

00:03:57.368 --> 00:03:58.350
I'll tell you.
- For real.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.080
- On 'All Stars', all the
people that you know and love,

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.790
from all over the world, who have won

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.290
and come close to winning, come back.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.170
People like Terry Fator, and Kodi Lee.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.230
But, you know, Avery,
- Avery Dixon!

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.063
- Yeah.

00:04:11.063 --> 00:04:11.896
Your golden buzzer from this year.

00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:14.460
When you see a young man hit the stage

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.000
and not be sure about his place in life,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.310
let alone on our stage.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.800
I watched him, and I
think a big part of it

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.440
was because of you and
the words of encouragement

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.273
that you give him.

00:04:26.273 --> 00:04:30.150
I watched this kid just
blossom into, I believe,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.070
is a future superstar.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.500
But into the human being and the man

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.560
that he never dreamed of
being, because of you.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.333
- But, isn't it amazing to watch?

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.480
The first time he came
out there he was in tears

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.180
because he was being bullied at school.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.910
He had no confidence in his talent.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.330
And then to turn around and become one of

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.600
the premier saxophonist
in the Country right now.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.190
He's only 21 years old,

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.379
and he could be the best
ever by the time he's done.

00:04:59.379 --> 00:05:00.212
(audience clapping)
You know what I mean?

00:05:00.212 --> 00:05:01.577
That's what 'AGT' does.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.960
- He didn't want to be on the show.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.660
His mother signed him up for the show.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.070
He couldn't even talk,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.800
and now you are,
legitimately, his big brother.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.700
- I am.
- [Howie] And you are there

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.533
for him.

00:05:13.983 --> 00:05:15.689
And you could see that connection.

00:05:15.689 --> 00:05:16.800
- And, he's back on 'All Stars'.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.722
- [Howie] Yes, he's back on 'All Stars'.

00:05:17.722 --> 00:05:18.555
- Which is so amazing.

00:05:18.555 --> 00:05:20.160
- By just watching you.
(audience clapping)

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.410
We have a great time on 'AGT'.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.683
What is, Simon and Heidi aren't
here to defend themselves,

00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:29.033
- Let's talk about it.
- Let's spill some tea.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.170
But it is a weird place.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.360
- Let's feel a tangerine, for Simon.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.193
- That's another thing.

00:05:34.193 --> 00:05:35.880
Simon is always, I don't know.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.200
You gotta watch the show really closely,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.270
'cause he's always just
finishing the tangerine.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.300
But, his whole chair is
just filled with peels.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.440
- Just peels.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.540
Everybody's trying to get what it is.

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.640
It smells all nice and effervescent
over there, like citrus.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.473
- That's me.

00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:50.070
But Simon is also.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.670
No, I'm effervescent and citrus.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.500
It is just a fun place to be.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.840
That brings me to the
book that you just wrote.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.640
Because people look at you,

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.040
and you seem like the
tough guy and the big guy.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.120
And you talk in the book about
what it means to be tough.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.200
Right?
- Yes.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.403
- Talk a little bit about that.

00:06:08.403 --> 00:06:09.660
They want me to hold up the book.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:10.493
Oh, here it is.

00:06:10.493 --> 00:06:11.843
- Oh, it's first of all,
- Here it is.

00:06:12.846 --> 00:06:13.679
- Where I'm from,

00:06:13.679 --> 00:06:14.512
- Where am I, there.
- I'm from Flint, Michigan,

00:06:14.512 --> 00:06:17.340
and there was a whole
thing about being tough.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.850
And being tough was about
being able to beat people up,

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.260
being able to intimidate people,

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.630
being able to be this
big dude on the block.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.390
But I found that being tough was really

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.700
all about helping people.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.700
It was really about helping
people reach their goals.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.980
And I remember having to have this shift,

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.280
and this is one reason why
I write books all the time,

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.370
simply because all my books
are to my 12 year old self.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.640
And 'Terry's Crew' was really about me

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.280
holding onto my dreams,
but more importantly,

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.500
finding the people that supported me.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:53.610
I dedicate this book to my art teacher.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.800
His name was, Dwight Eichelberg.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:59.010
And he believed in me when
I didn't believe in myself.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.140
He filled out all the applications,

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.760
took pictures of my artwork,

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:05.250
and got me two different scholarships.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.184
And I was like, "What
are you talking about?"

00:07:07.184 --> 00:07:08.017
(audience clapping)
And he was like,

00:07:08.017 --> 00:07:10.327
"Terry, you can do it."

00:07:10.327 --> 00:07:11.647
"You are amazing."

00:07:11.647 --> 00:07:12.900
"I believe in you."

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:13.740
And I couldn't believe.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.570
And I remember he was a corn farmer

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.910
from rural Michigan, and
everybody called him corny.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.130
They were like, "Oh, Mr.
Eichelberg's so corny."

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.967
But he was like, "Terry," he said,

00:07:21.967 --> 00:07:23.790
"you are better than I am,

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.257
and I want to see that you make it."

00:07:25.257 --> 00:07:26.370
And I'm like,
- Wow.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.570
it's really what this is about.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.540
It's about finding the
people that believe in you

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.070
and can help you get there.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.750
That's what 'Terry's Crew' is all about.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.150
And this is what I want
everybody out there,

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.800
- Support.
- kids and adults, to know.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:41.283
- The support.
(audience clapping)

